  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Kejriwal slams BJP-SAD alliance, says AAP's ties are with Punjab's people",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/kejriwal-slams-bjp-sad-alliance-says-aap-s-ties-are-with-punjab-s-people-126112400483_1.html",
      "description": "Aam Aadmi Party (AAP) national convenor Arvind Kejriwal on Tuesday hit out at the BJP over its alliance with the Shiromani Akali Dal (SAD) for the Punjab Assembly polls early next year, saying the BJP could join hands with any party out of greed for power.\nHe also asserted that the AAP's alliance was with the women, Scheduled Caste community, farmers and traders of Punjab.\nReacting to the announcement of the SAD-BJP alliance, Kejriwal said the two parties had repeatedly come together and parted ways for political interests.\n\"Sometimes they come together, sometimes they separate and then come together again. Our alliance is with the people of Punjab. We are working for the development of the state,\" Kejriwal said.\nHe said the people of Punjab have witnessed the work done by the Bhagwant Mann-led AAP government over the past five years. Kejriwal said the AAP government has been trying to address the problems affecting the state for several decades.\nPeople of Punjab have not forgotte",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-24T10:06:46"
    },
    {
      "title": "BJP-SAD to contest Punjab polls together, but ghost of farm laws persists",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/elections/assembly-election/sad-bjp-alliance-punjab-assembly-election-2027-amit-shah-sukhbir-badal-126112400517_1.html",
      "description": "Amit Shah said the Akali Dal would remain the senior partner in Punjab as the former allies revived a partnership broken in 2020 over the three farm laws",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-24T09:26:48"
    },
    {
      "title": "Shiromani Akali Dal back in NDA fold, to fight Punjab polls with BJP",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/elections/assembly-election/punjab-assembly-elections-2027-bjp-sad-akali-dal-sukhbir-badal-amit-shah-seat-sharing-126112400368_1.html",
      "description": "The BJP and SAD ended their 24-year alliance in September 2020 after the Akali Dal quit the NDA over the Centre's three farm laws, which were later withdrawn",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-24T07:37:56"
